The proposed solution meets the requirements for quality and relevance, compliance with regulatory requirements, level of security, data sovereignty, quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI, total cost of the solution, consideration of environmental issues, and capacity for innovation. We are confident that our Atelier platform, hosted on the Sovereign HDS tier of OuraneCloud, will provide the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) with an intelligent assistance tool that supports hospital staff in their clinical-administrative activities while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and minimizing environmental impact. The estimated global budget for the project is €900,000 over 5 years, which we believe can be optimized to achieve a gross margin within our target range of 25% to 35%.
